Shared-handle open back-off (bugfix round 0.7). A block whose header was usable but whose handles failed to open
(OpenSharedHandle, or a check of what it opened) was opened again on every acquire, so every frame, for as long as
the producer's handles stayed unusable: up to one OpenSharedHandle per slot and fence of the mask, depth
(0035), motion (0036) and HUD (0049) blocks a frame on the render path. Each block now tries a generation that
failed again at most once a retry interval (retry_milliseconds, 1 s, as a missing block is looked for); a new
generation is tried at once. Counted: open_failures and open_retry_waits per block (stats).
Also the GPU stats sampler (0007) loads gdi32.dll from System32 only (LoadLibraryExW, LOAD_LIBRARY_SEARCH_SYSTEM32).

